  "correction": "An earlier draft called L*FL observer energy, FQ/r radial pressure, the chain-rule radius derivative angular pressure, and beta*Q*FQ a mode-channel current. Those are Hamiltonian derivatives. Observer energy is FL/r. Stresses are rho, p_r, p_perp, j below. beta*Q*FQ is the shift/pressure cross term in the coordinate flux. FQ*Qdot is coordinate metric work and stays nonzero when K_r = K_perp = 0.",
